# Git normalizes the line endings of text files to LF in the repository. Without the text
# attribute a checkout with CRLF line endings (core.autocrlf=true) looks
# modified to git inside a Linux container.
* text=auto
# Go sources keep LF in every checkout: gofmt in the oracle container lists a file with CRLF
# line endings as unformatted (docs/design/eng-oracle.md, "Launcher").
*.go text eol=lf
# The empty form of pending.textproto keeps LF in every checkout: a test compares the form that eng/difftest writes with
# this file byte for byte, and the form has LF line ends (docs/design/eng-difftest.md, "Known signatures and the corpus").
tests/Great.Parts.Cel.Conformance/Regression/pending.textproto text eol=lf
# The generated Unicode tables and the reference of Go keep LF in every checkout: eng/unicode --check compares the bytes of the files,
# and the tests read the reference as a file (docs/design/unicode-tables.md, "The form of the output").
src/Great.Parts.Cel/Library/Unicode/*.g.cs text eol=lf
eng/unicode/reference/go-1.27.3.txt text eol=lf
# The corpus of RE2 keeps LF in every checkout: the test compares the hash of the bytes of the file that Go ships
# (tests/Great.Parts.Cel.Tests/Regex/Re2SearchCorpusTests.cs).
tests/Great.Parts.Cel.Tests/Regex/Data/re2-search.txt text eol=lf
